{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "GEN",
  "chapter": 32,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Jacob went on his way, and the angels of God met him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when Jacob saw them, he said, This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " God's host: and he called the name of that place Mahanaim.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Jacob sent messengers before him to Esau his brother, to the land of Seir, the country of Edom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he commanded them, saying, Thus shall ye speak to my lord Esau: Thy servant Jacob saith thus, I have sojourned with Laban, and stayed there till now:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I have oxen, and asses, flocks, and men-servants, and women-servants: and I have sent to tell my lord, that I may find grace in thy sight.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the messengers returned to Jacob, saying, We came to thy brother Esau, and also he is coming to meet thee, and four hundred men with him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Jacob was greatly afraid, and distressed: and he divided the people that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with him, and the flocks, and herds, and camels, into two bands;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And said, If Esau shall come to the one company, and smite it, then the other company which is left, will escape.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Jacob said, O God of my father Abraham, and God of my father Isaac, the LORD who saidst to me, Return to thy country, and to thy kindred, and I will deal well with thee;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I am not worthy of the least of all the mercies, and of all the truth, which thou hast shown to thy servant: for with my staff I passed over this Jordan, and now I am become two bands.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Deliver me, I pray thee, from the hand of my brother, from the hand of Esau: for I fear him, lest he shall come and smite me, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the mother with the children.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou saidst, I will surely do thee good, and make thy seed as the sand of the sea, which cannot be numbered for multitude.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he lodged there that same night; and took of that which came to his hand a present for Esau, his brother;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Two hundred she-goats, and twenty he-goats, two hundred ewes and twenty rams,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thirty milch camels with their colts, forty cows and ten bulls, twenty she-asses and ten foals.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he delivered ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " into the hand of his servants, every drove by themselves; and said to his servants, Pass over before me, and put a space betwixt drove and drove.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he commanded the foremost, saying, When Esau, my brother, meeteth thee, and asketh thee, saying, Whose ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou? and whither goest thou? and whose ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " these before thee?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then thou shalt say, They ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy servant Jacob's: it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a present sent to my lord Esau: and behold also he ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " behind us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And so he commanded the second, and the third, and all that followed the droves, saying, In this manner shall ye speak to Esau, when ye find him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And say ye moreover, Behold, thy servant Jacob ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " behind us. For he said, I will appease him with the present that goeth before me, and afterward I will see his face; peradventure he will accept of me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So the present went over before him; and he himself lodged that night in the company.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he arose that night, and took his two wives, and his two women-servants, and his eleven sons, and passed over the ford Jabbok.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he took them, and sent them over the brook, and sent over that which he had.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Jacob was left alone; and there wrestled a man with him, until the breaking of the day.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when he saw that he prevailed not against him, he touched the hollow of his thigh: and the hollow of Jacob's thigh was out of joint, as he wrestled with him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said, Let me go, for the day breaketh; And he said, I will not let thee go, except thou bless me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said to him, What ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy name? And he said, Jacob.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said, Thy name shall be called no more Jacob, but Israel: for as a prince hast thou power with God, and with men, and hast prevailed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Jacob asked ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and said, Tell ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "me",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", I pray thee, thy name: And he said, why ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou dost ask after my name? and he blessed him there.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Jacob called the name of the place Peniel: for I have seen God face to face, and my life is preserved.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And as he passed over Penuel the sun rose upon him, and he halted upon his thigh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.32.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.32.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore the children of Israel eat not ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the sinew which shrunk, which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon the hollow of the thigh, to this day; because he touched the hollow of Jacob's thigh in the sinew that shrunk.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
